{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5vSHqiPkQ9EgHTh5rn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The signup button no longer has a fixed width, so it should fit a 375px screen. I haven't seen it render, though. Bash was denied in this session, so I couldn't run the page or the tests.\n\n**Cause:** `.cta` in `styles.css` had `width: 420px` and `white-space: nowrap`. On a 375px phone the card's content box is about 343px, so the button ran past the edge and the label couldn't wrap.\n\n**Change (only `styles.css`):**\n- `display: inline-block` → `display: block`\n- `width: 420px` → `width: 100%` with `max-width: 420px`, so it fills the phone width and stays 420px on desktop.\n- Added `box-sizing: border-box`. Without it, the padding and border would push a 100%-wide button past the card edge.\n- `white-space: nowrap` → `overflow-wrap: break-word`, so the long label wraps onto two lines.\n\nOne visible side effect: on desktop the button's total width is now 420px including padding and border. Before, it was 472px and already wider than the card's 448px content area.\n\n🧾 allegedly · the signup button fits within 375px width after the CSS change · to check: open `index.html` in a browser with devices emulation at 375px wide (or run `npx serve .` and check the button's bounding box doesn't exceed the viewport). I did not run this."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1176,"cache_read_input_tokens":25005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1176},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7aa1dcae-1ebf-45db-8794-70abfc81b5b9","uuid":"5f3d23d1-8dc6-4b50-9500-79ce022e6aaa","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:39:36.797Z","reque